cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Automate QuICR (Quality Improvement Chart Review)"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2025-05-01"
license: Apache-2.0
url: "https://github.com/MorrisGlr/Automate-QuICR"
authors:
  - family-names: Aguilar
    given-names: Morris A.
    orcid: ""
abstract: >-
  QuICR is an LLM-driven retrospective chart review tool for primary care
  quality improvement. It takes EMR text, generates structured QI feedback
  using OpenAI structured outputs, enriches with medication NER and real-world
  drug pricing, and produces professional PDF reports. The tool reduces
  chart review time from 1-2 hours to under 1 minute at less than $0.01 per
  review, enabling quality improvement at scale.
keywords:
  - clinical informatics
  - quality improvement
  - large language models
  - electronic medical records
  - natural language processing
  - primary care
  - chart review
